    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44634" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏlĭpūga</span></b> ,
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a kind of venomous ant</i> (or, acc. to
			Solinus, <i>a kind of venomous spider</i>), <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 4,
				29, § 92</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22, 25, 81, §
			163</span></i>. —Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solpūga</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			837</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">soli-pugna</span></b> , acc. to
			Fest. pp. 300 and 301 Müll.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏlĭfūga</span></b> ,
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 4, 3</span></i> and 6; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salpūga</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 4,
				29, § 92</span></i>.</div>
